 "result_text": "`idna.decode(b'\\x8d\\xd2')` now raises `idna.IDNAError('Invalid ASCII in A-label')` instead of `UnicodeDecodeError`. I ran the issue's input and a second malformed input, `b'xn--a\\x8d'`, and both raise `IDNAError`. I didn't run the repo's test suite.\n\nAll the changes are in `idna/core.py`:\n- **`decode()`:** the initial ASCII decode of bytes input is now wrapped.\n- **`encode()`:** it had the same unguarded ASCII decode, so I wrapped it the same way.\n- **`ulabel()`:** the punycode decode there can also raise `UnicodeError` on malformed A-labels. It now raises `IDNAError('Invalid A-label')` instead. I didn't test that path directly.\n\n`IDNAError` subclasses `UnicodeError`, so any caller already catching `UnicodeError` keeps working.",
